From: mrdidit <26687854+mrdidit@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: chipone: follow panel power transitions

Keep Chipone TDDI transfers within the prepared lifetime of a panel
referenced by the standard panel property. Defer hardware initialization,
drain IRQ and firmware/recovery work before panel power-down, and resume
only after panel preparation. Gate debug transfers and reset operations
while the panel is off, and reject gesture wake on this shared-power path.

Use the upstream DRM panel-follower API, following the lifecycle approach
in drivers/hid/i2c-hid/i2c-hid-core.c. Keep non-follower devices on modern
system-sleep PM callbacks and restore them if a suspend attempt fails.

Preserve the pinned ROCKNIX Chipone implementation in patch 0064; this is
a local lifecycle correction, not a replacement driver.
